1
00:00:04,822 --> 00:00:15,872
Set up appointment types and provider schedules — Scheduling ▸ Appointment Types · Provider Scheduling — Fix the configuration and most scheduling complaints stop happening.

2
00:00:21,206 --> 00:00:27,994
Scheduling ▸ Appointment Types is the configuration behind most scheduling complaints.

3
00:00:27,994 --> 00:00:36,220
Each type carries a duration, a colour and rules. Book that type and the calendar blocks exactly that much time.

4
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:50,167
If visits routinely overrun, the type is wrong — fix it once here rather than dragging appointments every day.

5
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:58,798
Set the duration to how long the visit actually takes, not how long you wish it took.

6
00:00:58,798 --> 00:01:04,752
The colour is not decoration — it is how a clinician reads a whole week at a glance.

7
00:01:04,752 --> 00:01:13,851
And whether patients can book this type themselves online is decided right here.

8
00:01:13,851 --> 00:01:23,163
Saved, and available on every booking screen from this moment.

9
00:01:23,163 --> 00:01:30,057
Scheduling ▸ Provider Scheduling is the other half — when each clinician is actually available.

10
00:01:30,057 --> 00:01:41,494
Types decide how long a visit takes. Working hours decide when it can happen. Both have to be right.

11
00:01:41,494 --> 00:01:48,455
Set working hours per provider, and the calendar stops offering slots nobody is there to cover.

12
00:01:48,455 --> 00:01:55,496
Time off goes in here too — booked leave removes the slots instead of leaving them to be cancelled later.

13
00:01:55,496 --> 00:02:02,126
Set Clinic Hours sits above all of it as the practice-wide envelope no booking can escape.

14
00:02:02,126 --> 00:02:10,196
Get these two screens right and the calendar largely runs itself. Get them wrong and you rebook by hand forever.

15
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:28,190
What you just did

16
00:02:28,855 --> 00:02:37,855
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
